at the always inspiring [Newspeak House](https://twitter.com/nwspk), with roughly 30 participants split into groups.\",\"4 slides and 20 minutes later I was reeling with new ideas.\",\"it was gone 11am and I had only had one tiny cup of tea\",\"using quarterly reviews to get everyone out of the office and bonding again\"]},{\"id\":\"neutrality_collapse\",\"verdict\":\"supported\",\"rationale\":\"The essay plainly takes a position and advocates for the workshop's patterns rather than flattening them into balanced framing.\",\"evidence\":[\"Make no mistake\",\"This is exactly what [Loomio](https://www.loomio.org/) was built for.\",\"There is enormous strength in continuous participatory change.\",\"I highly recommend their [future workshops](http://www.richdecibels.com/workshops/) to others\"]},{\"id\":\"even_jargon_distribution\",\"verdict\":\"supported\",\"rationale\":\"The clear judgment fits: specialized organising and tech vocabulary appears where the writer is discussing methods and tools, while the surrounding narrative stays plainer.\",\"evidence\":[\"horizontal management\",\"Make decisions asynchronously\",\"a tool for realtime communication\",\"a space for asynchronous comms\",\"a space for static content\"]},{\"id\":\"forced_synesthesia\",\"verdict\":\"overcall\",\"rationale\":\"The cited line is an exaggerated mind-transfer metaphor, not a cross-modal sensory mapping. It does not make sounds into colours, emotions into tastes, or abstractions into textures in the sense required by this category.\",\"evidence\":[\"I could almost feel his hard-earned acumen making its way from his brain into my own.\"]},{\"id\":\"generic_metaphors\",\"verdict\":\"supported\",\"rationale\":\"Both flagged phrases are generic, detachable figures rather than concrete metaphors grounded in this event's actual particulars.\",\"evidence\":[\"like a beam of brilliance from above\",\"the elephant which lurks in every room\"]},{\"id\":\"referential_clarity\",\"verdict\":\"supported\",\"rationale\":\"The clear judgment is defensible. Pronouns and definite descriptions are generally recoverable from nearby context, and no major antecedent confusion stands out.\",\"evidence\":[\"what you might not have heard about are the patterns and principles which the founders of Loomio use in their own organisation.\",\"we defined a challenge we were facing, worked out a “desired future” and “next steps” to get there together.\",\"The ideas we came up with were many and varied and largely inspired by the patterns above\"]},{\"id\":\"formulaic_parallelism\",\"verdict\":\"supported\",\"rationale\":\"The flagged construction relies on neat oppositions that sound finished without explaining the underlying criteria, so the parallelism is doing too much of the work.\",\"evidence\":[\"which can be more inclusive and less invasive; timely but not hurried.\"]},{\"id\":\"semantic_redundancy\",\"verdict\":\"overcall\",\"rationale\":\"The closing sentence is a concluding synthesis, not a redundant restatement. It broadens the essay from individual workshop patterns to the larger political value of decentralised teams.\",\"evidence\":[\"The more effective we can make decentralised teams the more positive change we will be able to deliver.\",\"This is exactly what [Loomio](https://www.loomio.org/) was built for.\",\"There is enormous strength in continuous participatory change.\"]},{\"id\":\"underspecified_language\",\"verdict\":\"supported\",\"rationale\":\"The flagged phrases rely on praise terms whose criteria are not named, so the category and examples fit.\",\"evidence\":[\"well planned and designed workshop\",\"such timely content\",\"There is enormous strength in continuous participatory change.\",\"Brilliant advice which might be hard for some egos to hear.\"]},{\"id\":\"context_leakage\",\"verdict\":\"overcall\",\"rationale\":\"\\\"Make no mistake\\\" is a common emphatic frame here, but it does not require a missing external conversation to be understood. The sentence works as standalone emphasis inside the article.\",\"evidence\":[\"Make no mistake [Rich](http://richdecibels.com/) and [Nati](https://twitter.com/lombardonati?lang=en), who delivered this workshop\"]},{\"id\":\"performed_candour\",\"verdict\":\"supported\",\"rationale\":\"The clear judgment is correct. The document does not lean on honesty-markers or authenticity boosters of the kind this registry item targets.\",\"evidence\":[\"I’d like to send a huge THANK YOU out to Rich and Nati\",\"I highly recommend their [future workshops](http://www.richdecibels.com/workshops/) to others\"]},{\"id\":\"vacuous_connection\",\"verdict\":\"misclassified\",\"rationale\":\"The flagged sentences do make causal claims, but the problem is unsupported assertion, not an unclear connector or missing logical relation. The relationships are stated plainly enough.\",\"evidence\":[\"to ensure everyone receives adequate support. Simple, effective relationship building which is bound to reduce conflicts.\",\"If you can clearly define and agree which tool/s you will be using for each of these three essential areas of group work, your team is bound to be more effective.\"]},{\"id\":\"genre_specific\",\"verdict\":\"supported\",\"rationale\":\"The detected genre of `default` is appropriate. This is a practitioner workshop recap/pattern-language essay, which does not match the listed special genres, so no genre-specific watchlist applies.\",\"evidence\":[\"\\\"format\\\": \\\"pattern-language essay / community organising\\\"\",\"# Belonging is a superpower - Patterns for decentralised organising\",\"It summarises a workshop from the founders of Loomio\"]}]}"}}
